    "id": "ACT-GRAM",
    "revision": 8,
    "title": "Highlight when, where or how it happened",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-shi-de-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Highlight when, where or how it happened",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "When an event is already established, 是…的 can focus on when, where or how it happened. The frame highlights a detail; it does not introduce an ordinary possession relation. In a positive sentence, 是 may naturally be omitted when the event and focus are clear; keep the final 的.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我是昨天来的。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ shì zuótiān lái de 。",
                "meaning": "It was yesterday that I came.",
                "audio": "29e540e2a048f3619e492c1c20e7ffb62d8d7a0f88df7b3407a5614cb1af287f"
              },
              {
                "text": "我是在学校学中文的。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ shì zài xuéxiào xué Zhōngwén de 。",
                "meaning": "It was at school that I studied Chinese.",
                "audio": "7099af6bc6d5df42778c1cd3b0b5fbdbf9bd40c832286649bd1f702cf12d12e0"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
